{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"2ee4b099ef137d9a","type":"group","x":880,"y":-20,"width":1820,"height":1320,"color":"2","label":"The Harbor Master"},
		{"id":"188745aebe7d8efe","type":"group","x":880,"y":4900,"width":1820,"height":1320,"color":"6","label":"The Sea Folk (locked until befriended)"},
		{"id":"f182dd7c79fbe99f","type":"group","x":880,"y":2130,"width":1360,"height":1320,"color":"1","label":"The Watch"},
		{"id":"d045cfee2c62cba8","type":"group","x":880,"y":3510,"width":1360,"height":1320,"color":"4","label":"Beyond the Wrath"},
		{"id":"347437f892771800","type":"group","x":880,"y":1360,"width":2280,"height":710,"color":"3","label":"The Anchorage"},
		{"id":"2ab5564b805d8065","type":"text","text":"## Harbor Master's House\n*A snug stone house at the head of the quay, its lamp burning late over ledgers and tide tables.*\n\n**Requires:** Stone Quay\n**Materials:** 20 building stone, 3 oak timber, 4 roof tiles, 1 glass (28 cargo, ~9,100 SH)\n**Labor:** 4,800 SH\n**Resident:** A harbor master\n**Effect:** Ship upgrades can now be installed at Rayskaya.","x":920,"y":40,"width":360,"height":480},
		{"id":"3daec8dea85232fa","type":"text","text":"## Careening Slip\n*A sloping bed of stone where a ship can be hauled ashore and laid upon her side.*\n\n**Requires:** Harbor Master's House\n**Materials:** 20 building stone, 6 oak timber, 2 pitch, 2 tar, 1 hemp (31 cargo, ~12,000 SH)\n**Labor:** 6,000 SH\n**Effect:** Long-term repairs can be made at home for Medium or smaller ships, with dry dock materials at half price (500 SH a day).","x":1380,"y":40,"width":360,"height":510},
		{"id":"81e047aa9039b542","type":"text","text":"## Dry Dock\n*A great stone basin, gated against the sea and pumped dry, deep enough to cradle any keel.*\n\n**Requires:** Careening Slip; Deepwater Pier (The Anchorage)\n**Materials:** 80 building stone, 8 quicklime, 10 oak timber, 1 iron bar, 4 pitch (103 cargo, ~26,000 SH)\n**Labor:** 24,000 SH\n**Effect:** Long-term repairs for ships of any size, with dry dock materials at half price. No shipwright fee if the crew has a carpenter.","x":1840,"y":40,"width":360,"height":540},
		{"id":"9a09d699453ffd31","type":"text","text":"## Shipyard\n*Slipways, sawpits and the smell of fresh pitch: the place where new ships are born.*\n\n**Requires:** Dry Dock; Sawmill (The Works)\n**Materials:** 20 oak timber, 20 pine timber, 2 iron bars, 4 nails, 4 sailcloth, 4 hemp, 6 pitch, 6 tar (66 cargo, ~70,900 SH)\n**Labor:** 40,000 SH\n**Resident:** A master shipwright\n**Effect:** Ship upgrades are installed for 10% less. New ships can be built for 75% of their market value.","x":2300,"y":40,"width":360,"height":570},
		{"id":"aeda6d66c337fa09","type":"text","text":"## Chandlery\n*Coils of rope, barrels of tar and every small thing a ship might want, stacked to the rafters.*\n\n**Requires:** Harbor Master's House; Ropewalk and Tar Kiln (The Works)\n**Materials:** 15 building stone, 3 oak timber, 3 roof tiles, 1 nails (22 cargo, ~6,200 SH)\n**Labor:** 3,200 SH\n**Resident:** A chandler\n**Effect:** Repair stores and ship supplies can be bought here at half their Bazaar price.","x":1380,"y":650,"width":360,"height":540},
		{"id":"b2106b0b75c4e349","type":"text","text":"## Mooring Buoys\n*Great painted buoys chained to the drowned rooftops below, bobbing gently on the glassy water.*\n\n**Requires:** Stone Quay\n**Materials:** 3 iron bars, 2 oak timber, 1 pitch (6 cargo, ~19,200 SH)\n**Labor:** 3,200 SH\n**Effect:** Anchors no longer foul on the drowned city. Large and Huge ships can moor safely in the cove.","x":920,"y":1420,"width":360,"height":450},
		{"id":"c72e2158c941635b","type":"text","text":"## Deepwater Pier\n*A long pier reaching out to where the water runs deep and blue.*\n\n**Requires:** Mooring Buoys\n**Materials:** 50 building stone, 5 quicklime, 8 oak timber, 1 iron bar (64 cargo, ~19,800 SH)\n**Labor:** 12,500 SH\n**Effect:** Two ships of any size can dock.","x":1380,"y":1420,"width":360,"height":420},
		{"id":"a95dcb8aebb202ef","type":"text","text":"## Trade Wharf I\n*A broad wharf set aside for strangers' ships, with a bell to ring when a sail is sighted.*\n\n**Requires:** Deepwater Pier\n**Materials:** 30 building stone, 4 oak timber, 1 nails (35 cargo, ~8,200 SH)\n**Labor:** 6,000 SH\n**Effect:** Visiting ships may dock, with berths for 2. The party collects docking fees at Port of Call rates.","x":1840,"y":1420,"width":360,"height":450},
		{"id":"62d7d5184b7a313d","type":"text","text":"## Trade Wharf II\n*The wharf grows longer, and the cove grows busier.*\n\n**Requires:** Trade Wharf I\n**Materials:** 40 building stone, 6 oak timber, 2 nails (48 cargo, ~12,400 SH)\n**Labor:** 8,800 SH\n**Effect:** Berths for 4 visiting ships.","x":2300,"y":1420,"width":360,"height":360},
		{"id":"9de2f0ae096702db","type":"text","text":"## Trade Wharf III\n*A forest of masts where once there was only still water.*\n\n**Requires:** Trade Wharf II\n**Materials:** 60 building stone, 6 quicklime, 8 oak timber, 2 nails (76 cargo, ~16,800 SH)\n**Labor:** 17,500 SH\n**Effect:** Berths for 8 visiting ships.","x":2760,"y":1420,"width":360,"height":390},
		{"id":"79835ea3522d3f99","type":"text","text":"## Northern Watchtower\n*The old tower at the tip of the northern arm, raised once more from its broken stump.*\n\n**Requires:** Stone Quay\n**Materials:** 20 building stone, 2 quicklime, 2 oak timber (24 cargo, ~4,100 SH)\n**Labor:** 5,400 SH\n**Resident:** Two lookouts\n**Effect:** Any ship within 2 hexes of Rayskaya is spotted.","x":920,"y":2190,"width":360,"height":480},
		{"id":"ceb74219d144ab57","type":"text","text":"## Signal Mast\n*A tall mast atop the tower, hung with the bright flags of the flag code.*\n\n**Requires:** Northern Watchtower\n**Materials:** 1 mast, 2 sailcloth (~3,200 SH)\n**Labor:** 1,400 SH\n**Effect:** Flag code signals pass between the tower, the dock and incoming ships.","x":1380,"y":2190,"width":360,"height":420},
		{"id":"12c1bbc9cba48261","type":"text","text":"## Cliff Battery\n*Guns set into the cliffs above the cove mouth, their muzzles trained upon the only way in.*\n\n**Requires:** Northern Watchtower\n**Materials:** 30 building stone, 3 quicklime, 4 oak timber (37 cargo, ~7,500 SH). Guns are bought separately (Ship Weapons).\n**Labor:** 8,800 SH\n**Resident:** One gunner per gun\n**Effect:** Up to 4 ship weapons cover the cove, firing as a stationary ship.","x":1380,"y":2800,"width":360,"height":510},
		{"id":"65079b006e85a7e7","type":"text","text":"## Chain Boom\n*A great iron chain that can be raised across the cove mouth at a moment's warning.*\n\n**Requires:** Cliff Battery\n**Materials:** 6 iron bars, 4 oak timber, 10 building stone (20 cargo, ~38,400 SH)\n**Labor:** 8,000 SH\n**Effect:** The cove can be sealed. An enemy ship must break the chain to enter (AC 17, 80 HP, damage threshold 15).","x":1840,"y":2800,"width":360,"height":480},
		{"id":"a4499c24763a6dea","type":"text","text":"## Stone Quay\n*Old stone from the drowned city, hauled up and fitted anew into a long arm reaching out across the still water.*\n\n**Requires:** Basic Dock\n**Materials:** 40 building stone, 4 quicklime, 2 oak timber, 1 iron bar (47 cargo, ~11,000 SH)\n**Labor:** 8,800 SH\n**Effect:** Three Medium or smaller ships can tie up at once. Every branch of the Cove begins here.","x":460,"y":2840,"width":360,"height":480},
		{"id":"05debdb8b38c7e1e","type":"text","text":"## Basic Dock\n*A single jetty of fresh-fitted stone and pale island timber, raised by the monk's own hands.*\n\n**Effect:** Owned from the start. One Medium or smaller ship can dock. Large and Huge ships must drop anchor in the cove.","x":0,"y":2840,"width":360,"height":360},
		{"id":"a4f86f7bfc24194b","type":"text","text":"# The Cove\n*The harbor of Rayskaya, and its gate to the world beyond the Wrath.*\n\n**Building:** Pay for the materials and the labor, and the work is done. Materials are bought at market and must be shipped to Rayskaya. Once the Quarry in The Works is built, building stone is free.\n\n**Residents** live on Rayskaya once their upgrade is built, and work for room, board and a share of the island's trade.\n\n**Requires** in another tree is noted in brackets.","x":0,"y":2150,"width":360,"height":630},
		{"id":"ef0124d4ac0fe581","type":"text","text":"## Courier Run\n*A swift little ship that slips out through the Wrath and back again with letters and news.*\n\n**Requires:** Stone Quay; a Small ship given over to the run\n**Labor:** Its crew, hired at Port of Call rates\n**Resident:** The courier ship's crew\n**Effect:** Letters and news travel to and from the coalition.","x":920,"y":3570,"width":360,"height":450},
		{"id":"d054850e0ee8a73c","type":"text","text":"## The Blessed Fountain\n*A basin of dark stone, its water made holy by the touch of the Storm's champion.*\n\n**Requires:** Stone Quay; Shady's blessing\n**Materials:** 10 building stone, 1 quicklime, 2 bricks (13 cargo, ~900 SH)\n**Labor:** 2,800 SH\n**Effect:** A ship sprinkled with its water is blessed for a single crossing of the Wrath. But anyone who gets their hands on the water can find their way in, and Rayskaya is open to attack.","x":920,"y":4180,"width":360,"height":540},
		{"id":"b33aed8f31349967","type":"text","text":"## Trade Agent\n*A counting house in a distant port, and a trusted factor to keep it.*\n\n**Requires:** The Blessed Fountain\n**Materials:** None\n**Labor:** 10,000 SH each time\n**Resident:** A factor, living in their own port\n**Effect:** Can be bought again and again, each time in a new APC port. Rayskaya's goods can be sold there at that port's prices, or goods ordered to be waiting there.","x":1380,"y":4180,"width":360,"height":510},
		{"id":"b2086154f101464a","type":"text","text":"## Kingdom Factor\n*A guest from the Kingdom, given a house of their own upon the island.*\n\n**Requires:** Trade Agent; a Kingdom merchant house agrees\n**Materials:** 20 building stone, 4 oak timber, 4 roof tiles, 1 glass (29 cargo, ~10,500 SH)\n**Labor:** 4,800 SH\n**Resident:** A Kingdom factor\n**Effect:** Trade Agents can now be placed in Kingdom ports. The Kingdom now has eyes on Rayskaya.","x":1840,"y":4180,"width":360,"height":510},
		{"id":"8cd892b7b97ef948","type":"text","text":"## The Sea Folk Storehouse\n*A weathered storehouse upon the raft, where strange goods from beneath the waves change hands.*\n\n**Requires:** The Meeting Raft\n**Materials:** 6 pine timber, 1 nails, 1 pitch (8 cargo, ~6,400 SH)\n**Labor:** 2,800 SH\n**Effect:** A sea folk merchant comes to the raft to sell their wares.","x":1380,"y":4960,"width":360,"height":420},
		{"id":"8d45c85b51b27a04","type":"text","text":"## The Calling Bell\n*A great bronze bell, hung deep beneath the raft, whose voice carries for leagues beneath the waves.*\n\n**Requires:** The Meeting Raft\n**Materials:** 2 copper bars, 1 iron bar (3 cargo, ~40,000 SH)\n**Labor:** 2,400 SH\n**Effect:** Ring it to summon the sea folk. When they find a wreck worth diving, they ring it back: a wreck rumor the party can sail to and dive with a sea folk guide.","x":1380,"y":5570,"width":360,"height":510},
		{"id":"09dd7000e9f9fa14","type":"text","text":"## Wrath Guides\n*Pale shapes in the swell, swimming ahead of the bow.*\n\n**Requires:** The Calling Bell; the sea folk agree\n**Effect:** The Wrath becomes safer for blessed travelers.","x":1840,"y":5570,"width":360,"height":330},
		{"id":"9dfc8dce7280fd49","type":"text","text":"## Safe Waters\n*Holy water carried into the deep, and kin at last allowed to come home to the cove.*\n\n**Requires:** Wrath Guides; The Blessed Fountain\n**Effect:** The sea folk can come to Rayskaya unharmed, and may settle in the cove.","x":2300,"y":5570,"width":360,"height":390},
		{"id":"2fd2520c380bb757","type":"text","text":"## The Meeting Raft\n*A broad raft moored far out in the Wrath, where the sea folk may come and go in safety.*\n\n**Requires:** Friendship with the sea folk of the Wrath\n**Materials:** 10 pine timber, 2 oak timber, 4 hemp, 2 pitch, 1 iron bar (19 cargo, ~21,700 SH)\n**Labor:** 3,200 SH\n**Effect:** A place to meet the sea folk, far enough from Rayskaya that the Wrath does them no harm.\n","x":920,"y":4960,"width":360,"height":510}
	],
